#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:2
msgid "LDAP Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:4
msgid ""
"Syncthing can be configured to delegate authentication to an external LDAP "
"source. Typical examples include Microsoft Active Directory and OpenLDAP / "
"OpenDirectory servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:8
msgid ""
"To enable LDAP authentication some configuration options must be set in the "
"advanced config editor. Under \"Actions > Advanced\", select and expand the "
"LDAP tab. The following options are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:12
msgid "``Address``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:13
msgid ""
"Set to the address of the LDAP server, with hostname and port. For example, "
"``dc1.example.com:389`` for standard LDAP, or ``dc1.example.com:636`` for "
"LDAPS. (See also ``Transport``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:17
msgid "``Bind DN``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:18
msgid ""
"This is the pattern for the bind user. The special token ``%s`` must be "
"inserted to represent the username entered by the user at the login prompt. "
"Typical examples are ``%s@ad.example.com`` for Active Directory or something "
"like ``CN=%s,CN=Users,DC=example,DC=com`` for standard LDAP servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:24
msgid "``Insecure Skip Verify``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:25
msgid ""
"When set, this option disables all certificate verification for LDAPS. Use "
"with care and only when absolutely necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:28
msgid "``Search Base DN``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:29
msgid ""
"Optional, base DN to use for user searches. See :ref:`groupmembership` below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:32
msgid "``Search Filter``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:33
msgid ""
"Optional, search filter to use for user searches. See :ref:`groupmembership` "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:36
msgid "``Transport``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:37
msgid ""
"Set to ``plain`` for unencrypted LDAP (port 389), ``tls`` for LDAPS (port "
"636), or ``starttls`` for Start TLS (port 389 typically)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:40
msgid "A simple setup might look like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:44
msgid ""
"Once these settings are correct, LDAP authentication must be **enabled** by "
"setting the authentication mode to ``ldap`` in the advanced GUI "
"configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:53
msgid "Enforcing Group Membership"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:57
msgid ""
"In some cases it may be desirable to restrict login to members of a certain "
"group. We do this by using a custom search filter that matches users who "
"belong to the group only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:61
msgid "We need to know three things to specify the required search:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:63
msgid ""
"The base DN under which users are stored. This can be something like "
"``CN=Users,DC=example,DC=com`` for AD, or it can be a specific OU for a "
"subset of users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:66
msgid ""
"The DN for the group we need to match, and the user attribute that stores "
"group memberships. This varies depending on the LDAP schema and layout, for "
"AD the membership attribute is ``memberOf``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:69
msgid ""
"The attribute that stores the user ID that the user enters at the login "
"prompt. Again this varies, and it can be either ``CN``, ``UID``, or "
"something else. For AD it is ``sAMAccountName``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:73
msgid ""
"With these at hand we can enter the base DN in the ``Search Base DN`` "
"configuration option, and build our search filter. The search filter needs "
"to match both the user ID and the group membership. For an AD setup with a "
"group ``Syncthing`` in the standard location, a valid search filter is::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ldap.rst:78
msgid ""
"(&\n"
"  (sAMAccountName=%s)\n"
"  (memberOf=CN=Syncthing,CN=Users,DC=example,DC=com)\n"
"  )"
msgstr ""

